# L §5.11 step 3: "A rule already beaten by an applicable rule (step 4) has its when skipped, so a read guarded by
# an exception is never reached"; step 6: "Only the winner's value is evaluated: a beaten rule's division by zero
# ... never happens."  zero = 0: the beaten rule's when and value would divide by it.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input zero: int
input one: int

def x: num at reader
  rule a beats b = one
  rule b = one / zero when one / zero > 0

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  zero = 0
  one = 1

ask q1: x law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: 1
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
